   194→            border-radius: 2px;\n   195→            text-transform: uppercase;\n   196→        }\n   197→\n   198→        .type-technical {\n   199→            background-color: #e8f5e9;\n   200→            color: #2e7d32;\n   201→        }\n   202→\n   203→        .type-opinion {\n   204→            background-color: #fff3e0;\n   205→            color: #e65100;\n   206→        }\n   207→\n   208→        .type-discussion {\n   209→            background-color: #e3f2fd;\n   210→            color: #1565c0;\n   211→        }\n   212→\n   213→        footer {\n   214→            margin-top: 20px;\n   215→            padding: 10px;\n   216→            text-align: center;\n   217→            color: #828282;\n   218→            font-size: 9pt;\n   219→            border-top: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n   220→        }\n   221→\n   222→        footer a {\n   223→            color: #828282;\n   224→            text-decoration: none;\n   225→        }\n   226→\n   227→        footer a:hover {\n   228→            text-decoration: underline;\n   229→        }\n   230→\n   231→        @media print {\n   232→            body {\n   233→                background-color: #ffffff;\n   234→            }\n   235→            .column {\n   236→                border: 1px solid #000000;\n   237→                page-break-inside: avoid;\n   238→            }\n   239→            .three-column-layout {\n   240→                display: block;\n   241→            }\n   242→            .column {\n   243→                margin-bottom: 20px;\n   244→                page-break-inside: avoid;\n   245→            }\n   246→        }\n   247→\n   248→        .update-type {\n   249→            display: inline-block;\n   250→            padding: 2px 6px;\n   251→            margin-right: 5px;\n   252→            font-size: 8pt;\n   253→            font-weight: bold;\n   254→            border-radius: 2px;\n   255→            text-transform: uppercase;\n   256→        }\n   257→\n   258→        .update-announcement {\n   259→            background-color: #fff3e0;\n   260→            color: #e65100;\n   261→        }\n   262→\n   263→        .update-feature {\n   264→            background-color: #e8f5e9;\n   265→            color: #2e7d32;\n   266→        }\n   267→\n   268→        .sentiment {\n   269→            font-size: 8pt;\n   270→            padding: 1px 4px;\n   271→            border-radius: 2px;\n   272→            margin-left: 5px;\n   273→        }\n   274→\n   275→        .sentiment-positive {\n   276→            background-color: #c8e6c9;\n   277→            color: #2e7d32;\n   278→        }\n   279→\n   280→        .sentiment-negative {\n   281→            background-color: #ffcdd2;\n   282→            color: #c62828;\n   283→        }\n   284→\n   285→        .sentiment-neutral {\n   286→            background-color: #e0e0e0;\n   287→            color: #616161;\n   288→        }\n   289→    </style>\n   290→</head>\n   291→<body>\n   292→    <div class=\"container\">\n   293→        <header>\n   294→            <h1>Agentic Coding Research Report</h1>\n   295→            <div class=\"date\">March 25, 2026</div>\n   296→        </header>\n   297→\n   298→        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   299→            <!-- New Products Column -->\n   300→            <section class=\"column new-products\">\n   301→                <div class=\"column-header\">New Products</div>\n   302→\n   303→                <div class=\"item\">\n   304→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/productbridge\" target=\"_blank\">ProductBridge</a></div>\n   305→                    <div class=\"item-description\">AI agent that automatically collects user feedback across multiple platforms including Slack, Intercom, Trustpilot, G2, and ProductHunt. Uses AI to organize, deduplicate, and help teams prioritize features based on user feedback data.</div>\n   306→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   307→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI workflow automation</span>\n   308→                        <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-18</span>\n   309→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   310→                    </div>\n   311→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Feedback keeps coming in, but it rarely turns into clear product decisions. Really like how you've made it more structured and usable.\"</div>\n   312→                </div>\n   313→\n   314→                <div class=\"item\">\n   315→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/gitagent-2\" target=\"_blank\">GitAgent by Lyzr</a></div>\n   316→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Git-native open standard that transforms your repository into your AI agent's memory, skills, and identity. Define once and run anywhere from GitHub into Claude, OpenAI, CrewAI, OpenClaw without reformatting.</div>\n   317→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   318→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow orchestration agent</span>\n   319→                        <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-19</span>\n   320→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   321→                    </div>\n   322→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Store agents in Git. Version them. Port them. Run them anywhere.\"</div>\n   323→                </div>\n   324→\n   325→                <div class=\"item\">\n   326→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/claude-code-channels\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code Channels</a></div>\n   327→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Control your local Claude Code sessions remotely via Telegram and Discord. Built on Model Context Protocol (MCP), it enables sending commands, receiving CI alerts, and responding to external events from your phone.</div>\n   328→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   329→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI workflow automation</span>\n   330→                        <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-20</span>\n   331→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   332→                    </div>\n   333→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Allows developers to interact with Claude Code through messaging platforms\"</div>\n   334→                </div>\n   335→\n   336→                <div class=\"item\">\n   337→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/cursor\" target=\"_blank\">Composer 2 by Cursor</a></div>\n   338→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Fast, token-efficient frontier-level coding model that plans and executes multi-file edits across your entire codebase. Ranked #3 Product Hunt on March 20, 2026. $0.50 per million input tokens, $2.50 per million output tokens.</div>\n   339→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   340→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   341→                        <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-20</span>\n   342→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   343→                    </div>\n   344→                </div>\n   345→\n   346→                <div class=\"item\">\n   347→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/claude-code-scheduled-tasks\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code Scheduled Tasks</a></div>\n   348→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Schedule recurring coding tasks with Claude Code across local desktop and cloud. Set repos, schedules, and prompts once for automated execution. Ideal for continuous workflows and agent-like development.</div>\n   349→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   350→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI workflow automation</span>\n   351→                        <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-22</span>\n   352→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   353→                    </div>\n   354→                </div>\n   355→            </section>\n   356→\n   357→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Column -->\n   358→            <section class=\"column whitelist-updates\">\n   359→                <div class=\"column-header\">Whitelist Updates</div>\n   360→\n   361→                <div class=\"item\">\n   362→                    <div class=\"item-title\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n   363→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   364→                        <span class=\"update-type update-announcement\">Announcement</span>\n   365→                        <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-13</span>\n   366→                    </div>\n   367→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">Updates to GitHub Copilot for Students - GitHub introduced a new GitHub Copilot Student plan, rebranding the free tier to create a long-term, sustainable Copilot experience tailored specifically for students.</div>\n   368→                    <div class=\"item-title\" style=\"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 9pt;\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-03-13-updates-to-github-copilot-for-students/\" target=\"_blank\">View Changelog →</a></div>\n   369→                    <div class=\"quote\" style=\"margin-top: 8px; font-size: 8pt;\">\n   370→                        \"They're rebranding the free tier as the 'GitHub Copilot Student' plan, which is just the budget version\"\n   371→                        <span class=\"quote-source\">Reddit - r/GithubCopilot <span class=\"sentiment sentiment-neutral\">neutral</span></span>\n   372→                    </div>\n   373→                    <div class=\"quote\" style=\"font-size: 8pt;\">\n   374→                        \"Multiple 'goodbye github copilot' posts suggest user dissatisfaction with the changes\"\n   375→                        <span class=\"quote-source\">Reddit <span class=\"sentiment sentiment-negative\">negative</span></span>\n   376→                    </div>\n   377→                </div>\n   378→\n   379→                <div class=\"item\">\n   380→                    <div class=\"item-title\">Claude Code</div>\n   381→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   382→                        <span class=\"update-type update-feature\">Feature</span>\n   383→                        <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-12</span>\n   384→                    </div>\n   385→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">Custom Chart Creation Feature - Anthropic announced that Claude can now create custom charts, expanding the tool's data visualization capabilities for developers using Claude Code.</div>\n   386→                    <div class=\"item-title\" style=\"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 9pt;\"><a href=\"https://releasebot.io/updates/anthropic/claude\" target=\"_blank\">View Release Notes →</a></div>\n   387→                    <div class=\"quote\" style=\"margin-top: 8px; font-size: 8pt;\">\n   388→                        \"4% of GitHub public commits are being authored by Claude Code, projected to reach 20%+ of all daily commits by end of 2026\"\n   389→                        <span class=\"quote-source\">X/Twitter <span class=\"sentiment sentiment-positive\">positive</span></span>\n   390→                    </div>\n   391→                    <div class=\"quote\" style=\"font-size: 8pt;\">\n   392→                        \"The Claude Code TUI app is pretty solid. I use it heavily and get great results\"\n   393→                        <span class=\"quote-source\">Hacker News <span class=\"sentiment sentiment-positive\">positive</span></span>\n   394→                    </div>\n   395→                </div>\n   396→            </section>\n   397→\n   398→            <!-- Technical Insights Column -->\n   399→            <section class=\"column technical-insights\">\n   400→                <div class=\"column-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n   401→\n   402→                <div class=\"item\">\n   403→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Malicious litellm_init.pth in litellm 1.82.8</a></div>\n   404→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   405→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   406→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   407→                    </div>\n   408→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">The LiteLLM v1.82.8 package was compromised with a credential stealer. Installing the package triggers it without needing to import litellm.</div>\n   409→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   410→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">security</span>\n   411→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">supply-chain</span>\n   412→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">pypi</span>\n   413→                    </div>\n   414→                </div>\n   415→\n   416→                <div class=\"item\">\n   417→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Streaming Experts: Running 1 Trillion Parameter Models</a></div>\n   418→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   419→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   420→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   421→                    </div>\n   422→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">Running massive Mixture-of-Experts models on hardware without enough RAM by streaming necessary expert weights from SSD for each token processed.</div>\n   423→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   424→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">llms</span>\n   425→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">local-llms</span>\n   426→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">optimization</span>\n   427→                    </div>\n   428→                </div>\n   429→\n   430→                <div class=\"item\">\n   431→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/t8/hypura\" target=\"_blank\">Hypura – LLM inference scheduler for Apple Silicon</a></div>\n   432→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   433→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   434→                        <span class=\"source\">HN</span>\n   435→                    </div>\n   436→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">A storage-tier-aware LLM inference scheduler specifically designed for Apple Silicon hardware, optimizing for the memory hierarchy.</div>\n   437→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   438→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">llms</span>\n   439→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">apple-silicon</span>\n   440→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">optimization</span>\n   441→                    </div>\n   442→                </div>\n   443→\n   444→                <div class=\"item\">\n   445→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/amelmo/proofshot\" target=\"_blank\">ProofShot – Give AI coding agents eyes</a></div>\n   446→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   447→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   448→                        <span class=\"source\">HN</span>\n   449→                    </div>\n   450→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">ProofShot gives AI coding agents visual verification capabilities to check the UI they produce, addressing a key gap in agentic coding workflows.</div>\n   451→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   452→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai</span>\n   453→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">coding-agents</span>\n   454→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ui</span>\n   455→                    </div>\n   456→                </div>\n   457→\n   458→                <div class=\"item\">\n   459→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://jakesaunders.dev/bored-of-ai\" target=\"_blank\">Is Anybody Else Bored of Talking About AI?</a></div>\n   460→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   461→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-discussion\">Discussion</span>\n   462→                        <span class=\"source\">HN</span>\n   463→                    </div>\n   464→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">A discussion post exploring AI fatigue and whether the constant AI discourse is becoming tiresome for the developer community.</div>\n   465→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   466→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai</span>\n   467→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">culture</span>\n   468→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">opinion</span>\n   469→                    </div>\n   470→                </div>\n   471→\n   472→                <div class=\"item\">\n   473→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">The Definition of 'Slop' in AI Content</a></div>\n   474→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   475→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   476→                        <span class=\"source\">Neurotica</span>\n   477→                    </div>\n   478→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">Slop is defined as something that takes more human effort to consume than it took to produce. When a coworker sends raw AI output without review, they're disrespecting the recipient's time.</div>\n   479→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   480→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n   481→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">generative-ai</span>\n   482→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">slop</span>\n   483→                    </div>\n   484→                </div>\n   485→\n   486→                <div class=\"item\">\n   487→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">The Real Work of Software Development</a></div>\n   488→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   489→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   490→                        <span class=\"source\">David Abram</span>\n   491→                    </div>\n   492→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">The hardest parts of software development were never about typing code—understanding systems, debugging incomprehensible things, designing architectures that won't collapse.</div>\n   493→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   494→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">careers</span>\n   495→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai</span>\n   496→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">generative-ai</span>\n   497→                    </div>\n   498→                </div>\n   499→\n   500→                <div class=\"item\">\n   501→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Mar/20/turbo-pascal/\" target=\"_blank\">Turbo Pascal 3.02A Deconstructed</a></div>\n   502→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   503→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   504→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   505→                    </div>\n   506→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">Simon used Claude to decompile Turbo Pascal 3.02A and create an annotated artifact. However, a reviewer found the assembly annotations were 'hallucinated slop'.</div>\n   507→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   508→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">computer-history</span>\n   509→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai</span>\n   510→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">hallucination</span>\n   511→                    </div>\n   512→                </div>\n   513→\n   514→                <div class=\"item\">\n   515→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">SQLite Tags Benchmark</a></div>\n   516→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   517→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   518→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   519→                    </div>\n   520→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">Benchmark comparing five tagging strategies in SQLite with 100,000 rows, 100 tags. Indexed approaches easily outperform others, handling queries in under 1.5 milliseconds.</div>\n   521→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   522→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">sqlite</span>\n   523→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">benchmarking</span>\n   524→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">database</span>\n   525→                    </div>\n   526→                </div>\n   527→\n   528→                <div class=\"item\">\n   529→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Mar/19/openai-astral/\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts on OpenAI Acquiring Astral</a></div>\n   530→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   531→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   532→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   533→                    </div>\n   534→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">OpenAI announced acquisition of Astral, the company behind uv, ruff, and ty—three increasingly load-bearing open source projects in the Python ecosystem.</div>\n   535→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   536→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">openai</span>\n   537→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">python</span>\n   538→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">open-source</span>\n   539→                    </div>\n   540→                </div>\n   541→\n   542→                <div class=\"item\">\n   543→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.21430\" target=\"_blank\">DomAgent: Domain-Specific Code Generation</a></div>\n   544→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   545→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   546→                        <span class=\"source\">Paper</span>\n   547→                    </div>\n   548→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">Paper on DomAgent, which uses knowledge graphs and case-based reasoning for domain-specific code generation. Accepted to AAMAS 2026.</div>\n   549→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   550→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">code-generation</span>\n   551→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">knowledge-graphs</span>\n   552→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">agents</span>\n   553→                    </div>\n   554→                </div>\n   555→\n   556→                <div class=\"item\">\n   557→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Mar/18/snowflake-cortex/\" target=\"_blank\">Snowflake Cortex AI Escapes Sandbox</a></div>\n   558→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   559→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   560→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   561→                    </div>\n   562→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">PromptArmor reported a prompt injection attack chain in Snowflake's Cortex Agent. The agent executed malicious commands without approval.</div>\n   563→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   564→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">security</span>\n   565→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">prompt-injection</span>\n   566→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai</span>\n   567→                    </div>\n   568→                </div>\n   569→\n   570→                <div class=\"item\">\n   571→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.21362\" target=\"_blank\">AdaRubric: Task-Adaptive Rubrics for LLM Agent Evaluation</a></div>\n   572→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   573→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   574→                        <span class=\"source\">Paper</span>\n   575→                    </div>\n   576→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">Paper introducing AdaRubric, a framework for task-adaptive rubrics to evaluate LLM agents more effectively across different types of tasks.</div>\n   577→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   578→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">evaluation</span>\n   579→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">agents</span>\n   580→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">llms</span>\n   581→                    </div>\n   582→                </div>\n   583→\n   584→                <div class=\"item\">\n   585→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.21344\" target=\"_blank\">The AI Scientific Community: Agentic Virtual Lab Swarms</a></div>\n   586→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   587→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   588→                        <span class=\"source\">Paper</span>\n   589→                    </div>\n   590→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">Paper proposing agentic virtual lab swarms as a model for AI-driven scientific discovery, where multiple agents collaborate like a scientific community.</div>\n   591→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   592→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">agents</span>\n   593→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">scientific-discovery</span>\n   594→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">multi-agent</span>\n   595→                    </div>\n   596→                </div>\n   597→\n   598→                <div class=\"item\">\n   599→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.21272\" target=\"_blank\">The Library Theorem</a></div>\n   600→                    <div class=\"meta-row\">\n   601→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">Technical</span>\n   602→                        <span class=\"source\">Paper</span>\n   603→                    </div>\n   604→                    <div class=\"item-description\" style=\"margin-top: 5px; font-size: 9pt;\">Paper presenting the Library Theorem, which explains how external organization and knowledge structures govern the reasoning capacity of agentic AI systems.</div>\n   605→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   606→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">agents</span>\n   607→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">reasoning</span>\n   608→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">theory</span>\n   609→                    </div>\n   610→                </div>\n   611→            </section>\n   612→        </main>\n   613→\n   614→        <footer>\n   615→            <p>Generated with <a href=\"https://claude.com/claude-code\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code</a> | Data sources: Product Hunt, GitHub, Hacker News, arXiv, Simon Willison's Blog</p>\n   616→            <p style=\"margin-top: 5px;\">Agentic Coding Research Report - March 25, 2026</p>\n   617→        </footer>\n   618→    </div>\n   619→</body>\n   620→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
